@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
@accessToken = ACCESS_TOKEN
@secondAccessToken = SECOND_ACCESS_TOKEN
@gameId = 1

### STATIONARY — first roll
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-1

{"values": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]}

### Retry exactly the same accepted command — must replay, not create Roll #2
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-1

{"values": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]}

### Same key, different payload — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-1

{"values": [6, 2, 3, 4, 5]}

### STATIONARY — second roll (use a new key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-2

{"values": [1, 6, 3, 6, 5]}

### STATIONARY — third roll
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-3

{"values": [1, 6, 3, 6, 6]}

### Fourth roll — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: stationary-roll-4

{"values": [1, 6, 3, 6, 6]}

### REMOTE — client sends intent only; use this against a REMOTE game
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/roll/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: remote-roll-1

{}

### HOLD — after an accepted first roll, exactly five booleans
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/holds/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"held": [true, false, true, false, false]}

### HOLD — invalid before first roll or after third roll — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/holds/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"held": [false, false, false, false, false]}

### CHOOSE CATEGORY — backend owns player identity and points
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: choose-chance-1

{"category": "chance"}

### Retry the same accepted category command — same response, no second score
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: choose-chance-1

{"category": "chance"}

### Same category key with different payload — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: choose-chance-1

{"category": "pair", "pair_value": 6}

### Client must not send player_id or points — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: forbidden-owned-fields

{"category": "chance", "player_id": 123, "points": 999}

### Other participant attempts the current player's category — 403
# Define @secondAccessToken locally before running this request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{secondAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: foreign-category

{"category": "chance"}

### Action outside the caller's turn — 403 after the queue has advanced
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/holds/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"held": [true, false, false, false, false]}

### Reusing an already occupied scorecard field — 409 CATEGORY_ALREADY_USED
# Run when the same participant becomes active again after Chance was already used.
POST {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/choose-category/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: reuse-chance-new-turn

{"category": "chance"}

### Current authoritative turn state — can_roll is calculated, not persisted
GET {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}/state/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
